     "result_text_tail": "s $20M minimum. The only one-time cost the pack identifies is $7.5M of lease-exit costs, against the $25M limit.\n\n**Choices I made where I would have asked you** (listed on the last slide):\n- **No sales growth to FY2028.** All improvement comes from the actions themselves.\n- **Full wage rise.** I applied the 2027 4% minimum-wage increase to all store labor, which overstates the cost.\n- **Store split.** The pack only gives combined figures for the nine stores, so I split them evenly. That puts about $4.4M a year on the six whose leases end by 2027, which need no board vote, and about $2.2M on the three with longer leases. Those three cost $7.5M to exit, pay back in about 3.4 years, and need the board's approval in principle.\n- **Delivery pricing.** I assumed every e-commerce sale lost after the price change is lost to Harlow entirely, the cautious case.\n- **Delivery kept.** Home delivery stays, repriced, with its growth paused, to honour the owners' commitment.\n\n**Two things to check before the meeting:**\n- **Is FY2026 already over?** The pack treats FY2026 as the first year of the plan, but by February 2027 it may have ended. If so, replace the covenant estimate on slide 12 with the actual result before it goes to the lender.\n- **One-time costs.** Apart from the $7.5M lease exits, closure and other one-time costs aren't in the pack, so the CFO needs to estimate them.\n\nFiles are in ./:\n- deliverable/Harlow_margin_plan_board_Feb2027.pptx\n- build/ (scripts that rebuild the deck)"
    }
